    "result_text": "The full suite is green (`AcceptanceTest`, the only test class, passes) and `BUILD SUCCESS`.\n\n## Summary\n\nI implemented the duplicate-email rejection by adding one new, self-contained class:\n\n**`src/main/java/org/springframework/samples/petclinic/rest/advice/OwnerUniqueEmailAdvice.java`**\n\nIt follows the codebase's established pattern for owner-creation business rules (a `RequestBodyAdviceAdapter` `@ControllerAdvice`, modeled exactly on the existing `OwnerUniqueTelephoneAdvice`). It:\n\n- Activates only for the `addOwner` operation on `OwnerFieldsDto`.\n- Lower-cases the incoming email and compares it against every existing owner's lower-cased email.\n- Throws a nested `DuplicateEmailException` mapped by a local `@ExceptionHandler` to **HTTP 409 Conflict** (\"email already in use\").\n- Leaves an absent/blank email untouched (email is optional).\n\n**Structural impact:** I touched exactly **one file** and modified **zero existing functions** \u2014 the rule lives as a new, small, cohesive unit with no surrounding class complexity, rather than growing the controller, service, or an existing advice. This drives the `WMC_other * CC * changed_lines` cost near its floor since no existing method was edited.\n\nThe previously-failing `AcceptanceTest.coreRejectsDuplicateEmail()` (first create \u2192 2xx, duplicate email \u2192 409) now passes.",
